--- body ---
## Scope

Follow-up to the author's question whether the sitter can repair a failed
worker. Track a native Zotero recovery mechanism, not a plugin monkey patch.
`verification/SDT-PALGRAVE-AUDIT.md` identifies unresolved manager promises
after worker errors. The overnight plugin must not restart the shared worker
or submit another job while a native promise is unresolved.

## Acceptance

- Re-read native worker lifecycle and pending changes before implementation.
- On a proven worker death, reject affected pending promises and release queue
  processing consistently, then lazily create a replacement for future work.
- Distinguish actual worker failure from long citation-stage progress silence.
- Preserve other clients' lifecycle and define queued versus running outcomes.
- Exercise crash, initialization failure, message errors, concurrent clients,
  persistence failure and repeated worker death without infinite retries.
- No automatic retry of a pathological document without a bounded policy.
- Upstream filing requires separate explicit authorization.
